{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness","id":1386093,"title":"Sample locations in a city of World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T08:56:01-07:00","id":1386093,"title":"Sample locations in a city of World of Darkness","content":"There are a lot of 101 posts around (character ideas, plots, ...). The idea I had here was similar but for locations in a city. I plan on running a game of vampire set in a modern city. I looked up the city online, did my research and created the main vampire NPC's. I feel OK with what I wrote and prepared.<br /> <br /> Since I'm not an experienced Storyteller I need some help with &quot;random possiblities&quot; that my players could ask or interact or visit. There are some sample NPC's I found in the official books (police officer, vagrant, politician, even some ghouls, werevolves and vampires...) I need help with possible locations that aren't signature for a city but every (or almost every city) has them.<br /> <br /> There is a list I found in a Requiem book: Damnation City (link below). Its really good and it will help me a lot but there are a lot more &quot;shady locations&quot; that I can use for my city in a World of Darkness. Places where regular mortals would hang out, or vampires could use or other supernaturals would like to control/influence. That is where you fine people come in...<br /> <br /> Can you please help me fill up more of those locations. I thought of adding places like: library, museum, firestation, car wash, abandoned playground, shady bar, crack den ...<br /> <br /> URL: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1myNieV-7FW-AeUzRMLa4l88OJuFlQkfPCA0Oyb49Dek/edit#heading=h.32as74dpdiqx\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.32as74dpdiqx</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3864-refugee","name":"Refugee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:05:13-07:00","id":1386106,"title":"","content":"One place that I use at times is &quot;The Pit.&quot; Illegal under ground pit fighting between ghouls, vampires, and other supernaturals that the Owner manages to capture or otherwise acquire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:55:11-07:00","id":1386121,"title":"","content":"If I may make one suggestion, don't focus on a simple list of locations. It's unlikely the pcs will make it to every location, and you will have put a lot of energy into story ideas you're not going to use.<br /> <br /> (If, however, you can manage to railroad the pcs to all of them, in alphabetical order, you will be my STing hero!... jk)<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to focus. Focus on your story needs, and how your locations can propel the story forward. Maybe, you could describe a particular scene you expect to need a setting for? And, what role the scene plays in the overall narrative? Also, what you want the mood to be?<br /> <br /> <u>In the example below, note how the setting serves the scene, not the other way around.</u><br /> <br /> <i>The players have scheduled a meeting with the Primogen to accuse a nomadic fledgling of poaching on the coterie's domain, killing favored members of the herd. The coterie has been less than perfectly loyal to the Camarilla in the past, and now they come to the primogen... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8vwsu4-jFBw\" target=\"_blank\">hats in hand</a>... looking for the sect's rules to be enforced to the coterie's benefit. The pcs want the primogen to scare the fledgling into staying out of their domain. The coterie knows this could, in theory, lead to an execution, since the fledgling is in town illegally.<br /> <br /> You want the scene to highlight the similarities between the elders and the pcs, as they begin to sell out to the Camarilla. Also, there should be a mood of tenseness, since the pcs have previously scoffed at the rigid laws of the Kindred, but now want to use them to their own advantage. Will the elders gleefully declare the pcs outlaws, or will they be smiling like the cat that ate the canary, knowing the pcs have taken one more step toward loyalty to the system?<br /> <br /> For this, the meeting could be hosted in the first-class lounge of an abandoned train station. The arrival departure/board is still hanging. Instead of cities, it has the names of local kindred chalked on it, roughly in order of Status. The coterie notice they have moved up a slot or two. The lounge itself has been made presentable, but work is ongoing. Most of the coffered woodceiling is clamped into place and could fall at any time. The wallpaper has been temporarily pasted back up after damage from a recent rainfall. The rest of the station outside the lounge is so bad it should be condemned... only bribes and threats of city officials has presented such a fate. Dozens of flickering railroad lanterns light the space. Almost, but not quite, enough to require a frenzy roll.<br /> <br /> If the players fail to convince the elders, they (and the fledgling) are told to handle their own disputes, since justice is for the loyal. All the outcasts are politely, but firmly, shown the door. This leads down a long, crumbling concrete ramp into a baggage-handling cellar. A series of open archways put them on level with the tracks. Rats are fighting in the cinders outside. A gunshot and a siren can be heard in the distance.<br /> <br /> If the players convince the elders to help them, the scene will shift to the Ladies Lounge. This lies through a carved marble archway, and the room beautifully restored to its beaux arts glory. Gold chandeliers, flocked wallpaper, and mahogany floors abound. As the players walk in, however, they notice the floor is spongy and uneven. Is it even safe to walk on? The fledgling is lead through a service door and down a long ramp.... but to what fate? </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:03:37-07:00","id":1386136,"title":"","content":"Having settings to draw on though can inspire and some settings are the backdrop for several scenes. such as the club that the PC's mentor/Mwala owns will be a setting they visit quit often. I do agree that having the setting set the scene is a really good tool in an STs arsinal and i tend to use that a lot, but sometimes it is nice to not devote a ton of brainpower to create all of them and just pull a setting out of a hat. or have a bunch of settings to look at that may inspire scenes to come.<br /> <br /> Another reason to have some settings pre-set is to give the PCs something to strive or fight over fighting over a Setting can drive politics in vampire as feeding grounds buildings that have major importance politically and influentially in the setting is good to help create these dynamics even f the PCs have only heard of them and have never been their.<br /> <br /> But I don't want to stop by and not contribute. I will leave this system agnostic so anyone can use it if they wish.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><b>3rd Street Diner</b></span></div> <br /> <b>Description: </b>The diner on third street is a small but well known establishment. It was built in the 50's and quickly became a hot spot for the local high school kids to hang out at night as one of the few places in town to get a burger and dance to the jukebox that never seemed to stop playing. As time moved on and the crowed shifted with the years so did the type of clientele that met at the diner. Kids though stayed the main clientele but the amount of drugs that filtered into the place started to grow. The area around the diner faded into despair and the diner itself took on a less safe atmosphere. Now it is but a shadow of its former self. After shutting down in 2004 it became a boarded up shadow of its former self. Today it is a crack house of some repute owned by Tyson Woodly and his south-side crew.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible stories:</b> Several stories can come form this Tyson maybe a vampire himself and is influential in the south-side gangs. Maybe he is the Primogen or a street level vampire that buts up next to the PCs domain and is currently trying to politic to expand his territory by taking the PCs territory from them. In Werewolf this could be the hive of a BSD that is slowly tailoring banes and feeding them into south-side neighborhoods in the PCs domain and the PCs now have to worry about this Werewolf, they could help him and gain a powerful ally who may prove more trouble than his worth or hinder him and clean up their domain so that the blood will flow more freely with untainted blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:03:14-07:00","id":1386665,"title":"","content":"Two of my go-to standbys I've borrowed from fiction and television.<br /> <br /> <i>Shottle Bop</i>, from the Theodore Sturgeon short story of the same name, a small shop full of bottle of all shapes and sizes, containing all manner of odd and unusual things. Some are incredibly rare but mundane. Others alchemical marvels. And some are even seven types of impossible.<br /> <br /> <i>Curious Goods</i>, the store from <i>Friday the 13th: The Series</i>, a small out of the way antique shop, many of the objects within being haunted, cursed or otherwise tainted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-08-2020, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:10:23-07:00","id":1386693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness?p=1386665#post1386665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of my go-to standbys I've borrowed from fiction and television.<br /> <i>Curious Goods</i>, the store from <i>Friday the 13th: The Series</i>, a small out of the way antique shop, many of the objects within being haunted, cursed or otherwise tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. That show was amazing, especially given when it was produced and for how little a budget it had. It was definitely an inspiration for non-mythos Call of Cthulhu adventures, but I never thought about adding it to the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:47:02-07:00","id":1386762,"title":"","content":"I actually considered making a thread like this a while back, but never got around to it. Since we've got one now, though...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roadie's Bar</b><ul><li>50s-style bar and grill, with a heavy car theme. Walls are covered in license plates and photographs/illustrations of cars from that era (think fins, polished chrome, etc). A whole sports car (or at least its outside) has been cut in half and planted above the front door, back end outside and front end inside.</li> <li>Has a jukebox in the corner, but also has a tiny stage for musicians (comfortably fits soloist, uncomfortably sits a rock band). Mostly gets used by a rockabilly band that are friends with the bar owner, and have been performing Saturdays for as long as anyone can remember. Sometimes gets used for up-and-coming bands, but only if they can bend their &quot;sound&quot; to the bar's theme.</li> <li>Owner - the eponymous Roadie (nickname) - was getting up in years back in the 90s. If he's still working in 2020, it's as an old curmudgeon. May have been forced out of retirement due to economic downturns. How he stays in business is anyone's guess (read: mystery to be solved). <i>Definitely</i> knows where multiple bodies are buried. Nostalgic for the road-rolling days of his youth.</li> <li>Heard in the Background: &quot;Life is a highway...&quot;</li> </ul><b>Green Lion Antiques</b><ul><li>Reference to <a href=\"https://silenthill.fandom.com/wiki/Green_Lion_Antiques\" target=\"_blank\">Silent Hill</a></li> <li>Antique store, full of gently used furniture, knick knacks, pawned personal items, and general sentimental junk</li> <li>Owned by an alchemist (may or may not be Awakened, may or may not be Children of Knowledge/Solificati); sells herbal and alchemical substances from the back room, only to customers who specifically ask about it (and who have proper references from existing clients)</li> <li>Secret passage leads to tunnel connecting to property across the street</li> <li>Relies on revenue from alchemical sales to get by, when it isn't tourist season</li> <li>Will buy vampire blood, fangs, ashes</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:09:20-07:00","id":1386790,"title":"","content":"I'd only create locations that you know YOU as ST will be using to set scenes in, or as important locations of NPCs for purposes of havens, meeting places, influence centers, etc.<br /> <br /> Anything that is needed for random purposes (the PCs want to go to X, regardless of whether X is a new nightclub, bar, fish &amp; tackle shop, book store, motel, florist, etc.) can be thought up on the fly. Rather than put all the burden on yourself, feel free to go back to the PCs and collaborate on any essential features together. And you only need to put as many details as needed for the purposes of the PCs. All you need to do is veto anything unreasonable, and make necessary changes to better fit your setting. That way you can come up with things on the fly when you need them, the Players creativity can be used, and they feel like they are contributing to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-09-2020, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:08:57-07:00","id":1386806,"title":"","content":"I try to do a bit of a balance between both approaches that have been mentioned. If I have some locations I think there's a decent chance the players might want to visit but isn't necessary, I'll try to write a few sentences about it to help with improvising. A random name list helps with the improv, too. For maybes just having a little something to work with can help keep the flow of the game going instead of just trying to come up with everything on the fly. Obviously you can't anticipate everywhere they might want to go, but a few sentences can really help. You can also reuse some of them in other cities if the players never visited them before or maybe decide to develop them further into a plot location later if you have an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> For the firehouse, here's something that actually happened at one a few blocks from where I live now back in the '90s. The cops in the neighborhood would bust people for drugs, then take some of them and bring them to the firehouse where the firemen would sell the drugs again out the back. Oftentimes they'd just let people go after taking their stuff so there'd be no paperwork. The firemen and cops would split the money, which was all profit. They could even take and resell the same drugs multiple times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:14:15-07:00","id":1386824,"title":"","content":"I think developing locations can be useful in a modular sense. If you don't use a location here, you can use it somewhere else. Remember, the game world is an entirely constructed space. How it all connects together is up to the Storyteller. If PCs need to go to a place, you can MAKE a location be where the adventure is. I don't see that as railroading, so much as efficient use of tools you already have.<br /> <br /> Moreover, as DrHappyAngry hinted at, there are levels of detail one can get into when making locations. It could be a richly developed location with decades of history, a dozen NPCs, and secrets hidden in the very foundations. Or it could be a loosely formed spot with a general theme and some notes for details that could be fleshed out as needed. The latter is the approach I took with the entries I posted earlier. Brief, broad strokes, leaves plenty of room for improv or elaboration.<br /> <br /> (For a further illustration of this approach, I might recommend <a href=\"https://cyborgsandsorcerers.blogspot.com/2020/04/three-ways-to-make-better-hexmaps.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> from the Cyborgs and Sorcerers blog. It's about fantasy hexcrawls, yes, but its base conceits could be applied just as easily to an urban environment. Less rigid adherence to geography or distance, more about going into enough detail for functional use, and establishing connections to other locations. That's another important bit about designing adventures in any game: the players will be following breadcrumbs either way, so leave trails from where they are to places you've created.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:07:23-07:00","id":1386862,"title":"","content":"Well, if what you really want is some plug-and-play locations, here goes.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Furever Hearts Animal Shelter</b></u><br /> <br /> <u>Proprietors:</u> Joanie Zygumski, and Sarah Townley, DVM<br /> <br /> Ten years ago, Joanie retired from a corner-office corporate position. Sarah quit her job at a high-end vet office. She and Sarah used their nest-egg to pursue their lifelong dream of helping stray dogs, and they bought this place. Neither of them really knows much about fund-raising or grant writing. The couple have taken out mortgages on their house, and poured every penny into the shelter. They would love to run a no-kill shelter or simply fix the place up, but the funds just aren't there.<br /> <br /> Joanie is a tall, bony woman in her late 60's. She speaks with a clipped, suburban accent. Her movements are firm and intentional, like the military veteran she is. She has tan, heavily wrinkled skin, grey eyes, and a white buzz cut. She favors heavily patched khakis, and faded polo shirts. Joanie has a verbal tic: she repeatedly explains everything she is doing, as if those around her might misinterpret her actions. eg: &quot;Now, then. I'll get your file to maintain our records. Yes, here it is. Let me make a note of your purchase, and remind you of our special on dog adoption starter kits. We have a special on starter kits. You'll need one.&quot; Main Goals: Keep this place afloat, as it is clearly the last important thing she will do before she dies. Be the perfect wife to Sarah, as Joanie is terrified she will die alone.<br /> <br /> Sarah, an inveterate fan of the vegan commercial bakery around the corner, spent her sixties growing from curvaceous to chunky. This 70-year-old wears long, salt-and-pepper dreads which fall down her back. She moves with a calm balance, as if walking on an uneven surface. (In fact, she suffers from knee and hip pain.) At work she wears loose denim coveralls, work boots, a funny t-shirt (eg: &quot;Not all who wander are lost.&quot;, &quot;Visualize whirled peas.&quot;), and a spotlessly white lab smock. She speaks in soft, calm tones acquired from years of putting animals at ease. When angry or sad, she curls inward and steps back from the situation, like a wary stray. In unguarded moments, she hums or sings softly. Main Goals: Help as many animals as she can. Some, she reluctantly admits, can only be euthanized in the least painful way possible. Those animals who might possibly find loving homes must get them. She spends a good bit of her time reminding Joanie to be slightly less prickly to people she has just met. Sarah knows that if people could just see Joanie when she's relaxed, they would love her, too. Sadly, relaxed moments are a rare pleasure.<br /> <br /> Now, faced with advancing age and tarnished dreams, they bicker incessantly.<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance:</u> The shelter, a former auto-parts wholesaler, occupies a squat, cinder-block building in a light industrial zone. At night, when the warehouses and machine shops are closed, you can hear dogs barking from several blocks away. The lobby is tiny. Just a few folding chairs, and a chipped formica counter. There is a faint smell of bleach and urine in the air. A lush pothos plant vines its way across the drop ceiling, throwing random shadows on the concrete floor.<br /> <br /> Behind the front counter is an doorway which leads to a very utilitarian vet's office with exam tables, small holding crates, and shelves of medical equipment and medications. The office door to this room is propped against a far wall, its broken window awaiting repair. It has been waiting for six months.<br /> <br /> A further door leads to a large room full of staked cages holding recent intakes and dogs awaiting eunthanasia.<br /> <br /> Turning left in the lobby, behind a heavy metal door is a long hallway with cage after cage after cage of dogs available for adoption. Every cage is full, some double and triple full with dogs of every size and description. A slightly mossy hose and a scrub broom lie abandoned on the floor. All the cages have dog-doors leading to individual outdoor spaces. These are in plain sight of a large toolshed, behind which is an abandoned acre of gravelly, glass-strewn dirt which has been turned and turned. If the pcs are here at just the right time, they will see dog carcasses being dumped in an open grave with a small bull-dozer.<br /> <br /> <u>Story Role:</u> Last year, Joanie and Sarah interrupted a thinblood fledgling feeding on a recent intake. The dog was killed, but was in no pain. In fact, it seemed elated.<br /> <br /> Joanie, ever the realist, has opened their shelter as a feeding center for Kindred. They charge twenty bucks per dog, but only offer animals that are unlikely to be adopted. Sarah is appalled at this turn of events, and wants nothing to do with it. After a vampire brutally drained a shih tzu mix, though, she now insists on being present to ensure the feedings are done humanely. She stands quietly in the corner, sometimes crying softly.<br /> <br /> PCs are likely to come here for a desperation feedlot, as are other kindred in town. The shelter is like a watering hole on the savannah, where you never who you might run into. Most are ashamed to use such services, but it has become an informal, de facto quasi-elysium. Local elders are undecided about Furever Hearts. It does keep the groundlings fed and quiet, but too reliable a source of blood might lead to rebelliousness. Given the shelter's growing importance in keeping the lowest of low-clan vampires fed, there would be dire repercussions if anyone harmed the owners or the business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:19:36-07:00","id":1386888,"title":"","content":"The Nightmare Cafe.........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:47:48-07:00","id":1386894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness?p=1386824#post1386824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think developing locations can be useful in a modular sense. If you don't use a location here, you can use it somewhere else. Remember, the game world is an entirely constructed space. How it all connects together is up to the Storyteller. If PCs need to go to a place, you can MAKE a location be where the adventure is. I don't see that as railroading, so much as efficient use of tools you already have.<br /> <br /> Moreover, as DrHappyAngry hinted at, there are levels of detail one can get into when making locations. It could be a richly developed location with decades of history, a dozen NPCs, and secrets hidden in the very foundations. Or it could be a loosely formed spot with a general theme and some notes for details that could be fleshed out as needed. The latter is the approach I took with the entries I posted earlier. Brief, broad strokes, leaves plenty of room for improv or elaboration.<br /> <br /> (For a further illustration of this approach, I might recommend <a href=\"https://cyborgsandsorcerers.blogspot.com/2020/04/three-ways-to-make-better-hexmaps.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> from the Cyborgs and Sorcerers blog. It's about fantasy hexcrawls, yes, but its base conceits could be applied just as easily to an urban environment. Less rigid adherence to geography or distance, more about going into enough detail for functional use, and establishing connections to other locations. That's another important bit about designing adventures in any game: the players will be following breadcrumbs either way, so leave trails from where they are to places you've created.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much hits nail on the head. You don't need to write pages and pages of stuff for everything that might never get used at all. However, you can recycle some of the unused material for other locations in the future. Well fleshed out locations for important areas are great and help draw people into the story, but not every gas station or bar they go to doesn't need to be fully realized. Having a little bit ready in case they decide to hit a bar or talk to the local cops can be really handy and make sure you stick with the general theme and vibe you want for the chronicle rather than trying to make everything up on the fly and randomly go with something that doesn't fit thematically just because you had to come up with something on the spot. You do have a limited amount of time to spend developing the setting, so it doesn't necessarily make sense to fully flesh out locations that may not get used at all and don't have as much bearing on the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","user":"DrHappyAngry","date":".  fix missing word 05-09-2020, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:28:54-07:00","id":1386914,"title":"","content":"&quot;...or talk to the local cops...&quot;<br /> <br /> On that note, it would probably be prudent to make some sample police stations. While other locations can be hit or miss, Vampire games especially tend to wind up visiting law enforcement, sooner or later. Whether it's to subtly coax information, or to bust a PC out of lockup before sunrise.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Shrike Street Police Department</b><ul><li>Half the station is a modern, brutalist concrete structure. The other half were repurposed office buildings in Art Deco decor.</li> <li>Chief, of course, thoroughly subverted by the Prince (or whomever is in charge). Most of the force is corrupt.</li> <li>Owing to the above, the station has a leak problem, and we're not talking about the pipes. Most leaks are of criminal abuses (and the abuse of criminals), but it's just a matter of time until something Masquerade-related gets exposed in the shuffle. Some officers WILL kill to protect their secrets, given the chance, even if it wasn't related to the supernatural.</li> <li>Built on top of prohibition-era smugglers tunnels, one of which leads to lock-up. Kept around by vampires specifically to prevent Masquerade breaching vampire immolations. However, entrances to said tunnels have been accidentally (deliberately?) bricked up, as part of unrelated remodeling efforts in and around the station.</li> <li>FBI agents have a permanent office set up at the station, as part of cooperation between the Bureau and local law enforcement on a particular case. Aforementioned police corruption makes this arrangement a tense affair. FBI agents might also have their ears to the ground concerning &quot;unusual&quot; activity (read: may be connected, albeit tangentially, to SAD).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:46:17-07:00","id":1386919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness?p=1386914#post1386914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;...or talk to the local cops...&quot;<br /> <br /> On that note, it would probably be prudent to make some sample police stations. While other locations can be hit or miss, Vampire games especially tend to wind up visiting law enforcement, sooner or later. Whether it's to subtly coax information, or to bust a PC out of lockup before sunrise.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Shrike Street Police Department</b><ul><li>Half the station is a modern, brutalist concrete structure. The other half were repurposed office buildings in Art Deco decor.</li> <li>Chief, of course, thoroughly subverted by the Prince (or whomever is in charge). Most of the force is corrupt.</li> <li>Owing to the above, the station has a leak problem, and we're not talking about the pipes. Most leaks are of criminal abuses (and the abuse of criminals), but it's just a matter of time until something Masquerade-related gets exposed in the shuffle. Some officers WILL kill to protect their secrets, given the chance, even if it wasn't related to the supernatural.</li> <li>Built on top of prohibition-era smugglers tunnels, one of which leads to lock-up. Kept around by vampires specifically to prevent Masquerade breaching vampire immolations. However, entrances to said tunnels have been accidentally (deliberately?) bricked up, as part of unrelated remodeling efforts in and around the station.</li> <li>FBI agents have a permanent office set up at the station, as part of cooperation between the Bureau and local law enforcement on a particular case. Aforementioned police corruption makes this arrangement a tense affair. FBI agents might also have their ears to the ground concerning &quot;unusual&quot; activity (read: may be connected, albeit tangentially, to SAD).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonable advice, you generally have to deal with the local law enforcement at some point in time and having a framework for it in advance is a good idea. Example form a Dark Ages game, I had a city guard character background at hand in case anybody decided to chat up a guard. The Salubri Warrior decides to regale a gate guard with tales of his bravery and the guard mentions his exploits in the campaigns of Charles Martel. You can easily change that to something more relevant to your time period like he was deployed to Afghanistan/Iraq or Vietnam/Korea if you want to go further back. It does require a bit of research into the specific war they were in, but works really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:55:05-07:00","id":1386923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness?p=1386888#post1386888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nightmare Cafe.........</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you are a person of culture and taste.<br /> <br /> I was going to mention the all too short lived Wes Craven series, about a strange all night diner that offers people second chances, but I am forever unable to remember what the place was actually called in the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T01:09:34-07:00","id":1386931,"title":"","content":"Here's some of the ones I've used in my game.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Hawaiian Hut</b>: A shady no-tell motel that has missing neon-letters, a tropical theme in only the vaguest sense, and a general reputation as a complete shit hole. The Hawaiian Hut is notable for the fact its controlled by the <b>69ers</b> that are a local street gang that uses it as a brothel for their activities as well as a place to drug pot, crack, and opiods. Weirdly enough, there is a very nice set pair of rooms that are available for rent that are extremely luxurious, approaching 3 1/2 star level if not 4 stars. These are never rented out unless you know about them.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Scarlet Woman</b>: A strip club that is extremely high end with good music, lighting, fog, talented dancers, and a lovely neon-theme. The Scarlet Woman tends to host bachelor parties, business celebrations, and other works. Light prostitution goes on but the woman seem remarkably happy about the arrangement and speak of the owner in somewhat glowing terms. The place is extremely expensive but actually has been known to turn away guests like a nightclub or let in others for free.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>K-Witchcraft</b>: Witchcraft Joe runs a pirate radio station that operates out of the second floor of an old department store. Witchcraft Joe is a Gulf War veteran who looks and acts more like a Vietnam War veteran. He is usually on acid, pot, pills, or some combination of the three. Joe is a somewhat apolitical conspiracy theorist and actually has a fairly decent number of True Crime reporters as well as informants around the city. He lives in his &quot;office&quot; but seems to have a surprising amount of money to buy stories or give away people or bribe people to leave him alone.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Banana Mobile</b>: An absurdly kitsch van with an enormous banana on the top of it that sells banana ice cream and banana splits, theoretically. In truth, the Banana Mobile is actually a vehicle for buying illegal weapons around the city. Its operator, Morty, has a deal with gun shows and the local gun dealers that allows him to acquire whatever he needs before selling to the city's criminals.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>The Phantom Police Station</b>: Something so ridiculous that it can only be true. The Phantom Police Station is an entirely functional appearing police station that is completely run by criminals. They have police cars, uniforms, weapons, and their own collection of operatives that do work for the local crime syndicates as well as provide security on demand for those who will pay for it. The police in town are fairly certain that it HAS to be a real police station because that would be ridiculous otherwise, right? They have been known to interfere in numerous other investigations, take care of calls, and shut down things that would be uncomfortable. Prisoners who go into their cells also don't always come out.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Greenplace Security and Holding</b>: A detention center that has gained a great deal of business in recent years. The organization agrees to hold illegal immigrants and other individuals that are picked up by ICE officers as well as law enforcement. It's fairly an open secrey that Greenplace is actually a front for human trafficking with someone regularly buying up its detainees. Not only children and young women either but everyone. They're not often seen again either. Whether they're being sold to brothels, cartels, vampires, or serial killers--it doesn't matter to the people who take home an extra 60K per year.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The Magadon Truck</b>: A transport truck with a mobile clinic in the back. The Magadon Truck pulls into the homeless population camps for free check-ups, inoculations, and treatment every week. The Magadon Truck offers the homeless population cash payments in exchange for taking blood samples and giving them regular injections of perfectly safe materials. Members who get sick afterward often seek them out for more treatments, which occasionally ends in them disappearing.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Lucien's Coffin</b>: There's nothing more pathetic than a middle aged Goth, unless he's at Lucien's Coffin where the Nineties never ended. Men and women in their 40s put on their capes, leather, bustiers, and pancake makeup to go to one of the world's only Goth nightclubs that cater exclusively to soccer moms as well as corporate drones seeking to recapture their Hot Topic Youth. The Sisters of Mercy and Nine Inch Nails will never stop being popular here as it mainly exists as a place for casual hook ups, drinking, and marital affairs. The place has been described as a cheap version of the Succubus Club but the fact is that it actually is making fairly decent bank since the guests have disposable income as well as the owner owning the beauty parlor as well as costume shop next door. He also gets a cut of the &quot;Halloween crowd&quot; making use of the hotel across the street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-09-2020, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:47:43-07:00","id":1386961,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Pavello's World-O-Books</b></u><br /> <br /> Pavello's occupies a 1920's era bank building, with cracked terrazzo floors and soaring, yet leak stained, ceilings. The two-story arched windows face onto a busy retail strip a few blocks on the &quot;bad side&quot; of an urban university campus. The store is flanked by a tattoo shop, with ratty apartments above, and a three-story thrift store which specializes in used furniture, vintage men's suits, and bedbugs.<br /> <br /> Local lore states that every book ever printed can be found somewhere in this store, if you can only find it. There are whole rooms of publisher over-runs, used text books, and review copies. Stacks of Popular Mechanics, National Geographics, and muscle magazines dating back to the 1930s threaten to topple over right next to Estonian language translations of the Iliad, and tax codes from the Ottoman Empire. Somewhere in here, if you can find it, are a signed first-edition of Neruda's Cancion de gesta, a detailed map of the city's sewer system, and a Tamil translation of the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> There is, in fact, a strange logic to the stacks, if you know how to search. For example, there are two rooms of sheet music upstairs. One is filled with music Pavello likes, the other with what he calls &quot;crude abuses of a G clef&quot;.<br /> <br /> In 1974, Mr. Pavello left his job as a research engineer to take over his parents' bookstore when they retired. He has a regular income from several inventions, mostly early printing techniques for circuit boards. Despite being in his nineties, most locals call him &quot;the younger Mr. Pavello&quot;; his first name is a closely guarded secret. Pavello has amassed one of the largest collections of books on the continent. Unfortunately, his beautiful mind isn't what it once was. Pavello sleeps in the basement of his store, on an antique four-poster bed. One corner of it is held up with an auto jack. A family of rats live in the mattress.<br /> <br /> Pavello is a short man of thin build. He has an olive complexion, and stick-thin, arthritic fingers. Once or twice a year he dyes his hair shoe-polish black; between these beauty treatments he has varying lengths of white roots. He always wears a grey flannel suit, with the slacks pulled up to his chest. He walks with a foosh-fooshing shuffle. This is partly due to his advanced age, and partly due to the fluffy slippers he insists on wearing at all times.<br /> <br /> It can be difficult to engage Pavello in anything beyond perfunctory customer service, as he is painfully shy. Once you hit on a topic he enjoys, he will brighten and follow you around the store handing you related books, and cracking decades old dad-jokes and groaner puns. Be careful, however, if you are in his store in the hours straddling sunset and sunrise as he is prone to fits of rage in which he furiously restocks books, and throws small objects in frustration. There have been a few incidents with browsers, but no one has been hurt so far. In truth, he finds these times more frightening than witnesses do; these are his most confused moments and they can leave him in tears afterward.<br /> <br /> Pavello has a habit of opening and closing the store at odd times, though he always opens it when the sun is out and closes it during the night time hours. So, today he might be open 5pm to 4am. Tomorrow, the schedule is a more conventional 7am to 7pm.<br /> <br /> <u>Story Use:</u> The store is popular among undergrads and professors alike. It also has a following among local mages, who use it for coincidental research. This would be an excellent place for cross-species meetings for academic supernaturals. It's also useful for research, perhaps moreso than the nearby University Library.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:40:05-07:00","id":1386994,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Rotary Park Transverse Comfort Stations</b></u><br /> <br /> In a busy neighborhood downtown, five streets meet at odd angles. In 1890, tired of traffic confusion, the city tore down four blocks of tenements and built a massive roundabout with a large park in the middle. Ignoring the advice of writers concerned with redundancy, the city named the circle road &quot;Rotary Circle Drive&quot;. The park, however, was not popular at all. The problem? Crossing heavy traffic on foot made it too dangerous to get there.<br /> <br /> In 1935, as a WPA project, a transverse tunnel was installed. A small art-deco building on each corner held grand staircases descending three stories to a circular hallway directly under Rotary Circle Drive above. The floors were of inlaid terrazzo. Walls were covered in monumental mosaics depicting the myth of Persephone and Hades. Deep alcoves held lunch counters and news stands. Most spectacular were the restrooms. The walls were tiled in aqua-blue glass beads, ranging in size from a ball bearing up to a fist. The floors and stall panels were white marble.<br /> <br /> Three grand arches on the inner wall of the Transverse lead to a grand, curving staircase. A geometric waterfall cascaded three stories through the atrium of the stairwell. Visitors arrived back at ground level surrounded by planters, paths, and trees. A verdant oasis in the city met them. The Rotary Park Transverse Comfort Stations were featured in magazines across the country when it opened, hailed as an architectural triumph.<br /> <br /> The years have not been kind to the Transverse. Budget cuts in the 70's ceased maintenance, and forced the businesses to close. Drug activity in Rotary Park during the crack epidemic of the 80's led to the padlocking of the access buildings and the Transverse's full closure. Crosswalks were installed and all the trees in the park were cut down to make police patrols easier. Today, the park is a brick plaza, with occasional benches. It is so disused, the city is debating selling the land for development.<br /> <br /> The Transverse has seen little activity in forty years. City engineers inspect the structure every six months. Maintenance crews use the grand staircase in the park to store equipment and supplies. Otherwise, the murals are crumbling, the floors are cracking, and the copper fixtures are more verdigris than metal. There is no electricity. A six-foot hatch in a side room is rusted shut, but is beginning to crack. A swampy smell emanates from the city's main rain sewer beyond.<br /> <br /> <u>Story Use:</u> No other vampires have claimed the Transverse, but if your players can't figure out something to do with a 50000 square foot underground space in the heart of downtown, they should go back to playing Toon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:48:13-07:00","id":1386998,"title":"","content":"I will mention that Atlas Games's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/248629/At-Your-Service-Over-the-Edge-1E-digital\" target=\"_blank\">At Your Service</a>, for first edition Over the Edge, is a fun collection of locations (about three dozen in total) that range from the slightly off kilter to the rather surreal. <br /> <br /> Also, Bishopsgate from (CoD)World of Darkness: Asylum and the sample police department in Tales of the 13th Precinct can slot very easily into most American cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:37:40-07:00","id":1387045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1386093-sample-locations-in-a-city-of-world-of-darkness?p=1386923#post1386923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see you are a person of culture and taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your kind words. And to answer your query, it was known as The All Night Cafe.....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","user":"Gangrel44","date":". 05-09-2020, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:32:27-07:00","id":1387063,"title":"","content":"Something that I have rarely heard people discuss with vampires is long term storage.<br /> <br /> <b>Centennial Storage:</b> <br /> Located in a modern well kept industrial park, Centennial Storage offers 24 hour service with a variety of storage options from smaller closet lockers to large 25' x 25' rooms to your average customer. Their security is above average for such locations and the staff tend to have ex-military and mercenary backgrounds rather than standard rent-a-cops.<br /> <br /> A service that isn't advertised is that one of the empty storage lockers actually conceals a hidden entrance to an underground facility which has climate controlled vaults with air tight seals. Mortals and cainites alike can rent the above ground storage, but only kindred can rent the underground vaults. The shortest rental agreement for the vaults is 50 years, while there are accounts that are quite a bit older.<br /> <br /> If anyone comes around asking about a given kindred using their services, the staff are instructed to respond that the kindred used to own a storage locker, but cleared it out the last time they came by. Of course all kindred files point to the same empty storage space. No records are kept of what is in the vaults, just contact information and specifics for vault atmosphere, moisture levels and types of light installed.<br /> <br /> Depending on your game needs the storage location might be granted the Elysium status to ensure that kindred don't mess with each other. The underground vaults are excellent for any Thaumaturgy or Necromancy practitioner who want to keep their ritual space away from their haven, alternatively the ability to control the environment means that many kindred with older items can safely protect them against the ravages of time. A private library of first editions would greatly benefit from such a storage option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:40:50-07:00","id":1387066,"title":"","content":"<b>Kowloon Walled Alley</b><ul><li>Nestled between two large buildings, a space designed to replicate the famous Kowloon Walled City of Hong Kong, not unlike <a href=\"https://matcha-jp.com/en/1116\" target=\"_blank\">this (sadly closed) arcade</a>. Just on a smaller scale.</li> <li>Contains a small shop for buying East Asian imports (some of dubious legality), a vendor selling mostly authentic Hong Kong street food (some ingredients just aren't available in the west), and a corner stuffed with arcade cabinets.</li> <li>For reasons elucidated below, location hasn't had to pay taxes or stand up to city ordinance for a few years now.</li> <li>Far larger on the inside than the dimensions of the surrounding buildings would imply.</li> <li>A technomancer Marauder makes his home inside the space, which has slowly expanded following him moving in. An original resident of the famous slum, being made to leave and seeing his home destroyed broke his mind, turning him into a Quiet-addled Mage. Drawn to the minor attraction by means unknown, he finds it the only place that truly, naturally conforms to his cyberpunk view of the world. Originally an engineer by trade, the impossible upper (deeper?) reaches of the Reality Zone have become his lab, where he perfects his cybernetic inventions.</li> <li>Casual enthusiasts and cosplayers come to take in the atmosphere. Hong Kong expatriates and tourists come for a bite of familiar food or to grab some familiar products. Virtual Adepts and Etherites come to buy and sell materials and tech with the Marauder.</li> <li>Original creator of the attraction puts on a positive face, but is very aware of how much the whole thing has gone beyond his control. Deeply afraid of whoever the &quot;Technocratic Union&quot; he keeps overhearing about, and whether they'll come to shut the place down (or worse).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:13:06-07:00","id":1387124,"title":"","content":"<u><b>The Bauernbruderen Kolonie</b></u><br /> <br /> In 1680, a pietist, anabaptist sect in Germany fled religious warfare and economic disruption by fleeing to the New World. They established a farming colony which has lived separately from the secular world ever since. They speak an antiquated dialect of German, which modern German speakers can sort of understand if they ignore all standards of grammar and vocabulary. As a plain sect, they eschew all modern technology. They have retained 17th century working class clothing and manners. They live in tiny villages, with a total population of 2000 souls.<br /> <br /> The sect is governed by the Gemeinhaus, a council of a dozen elderly churchmen, who set the rules by which the community live, called the Ordnung.<br /> <br /> This is all very quaint and scenic. Dozens of cheap motels, gift shops, and all-you-can-eat buffets line Main Street. Teeming crowds of tourists from the nearby city spend their weekends here, wiping melted ice-cream off their children's hex sign t-shirts. Somehow, they manage to get lost in a five street town. Air-conditioned bus tours leave every half-hour. Don't forget to buy some shoo-fly pie for the guys at work on Monday!<br /> <br /> Humans aren't the only tourists. Beyond the boundaries of modern Muhler Borough, tourist honky-tonks give way to the Bauernbruderen communities proper. Rolling hillsides and endless miles of cornfields and bank barns overlook cobblestoned villages. Torches and lanterns light stone farmhouses and the tidy gardens which surround them. Horse-drawn buggies clip-clop from town to town. Elder vampires come here to forget the modern world and stroll through their memories. It's become common practice to transition recently awakened elders into the modern world here.<br /> <br /> The Gemeinhaus are aware of the Kindred among them. They view it as a regrettable necessity. The modern world would surely corrupt the members of the sect and intrude on their seclusion if the Anglischer Wampiren didn't intercede to help maintain isolation. In exchange, the Gemeinhaus arrange for sun-proof havens and a supply of healthy vessels. The blood of the Bauernbruderen youth are know for its remarkably clean flavor, free of tobacco, alcohol, preservatives, and chemical flavorings.<br /> <br /> Story Role: A sentimental favorite for elders looking to hold meetings, from romantic rendezvous to contract negotiations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","user":"Nosimplehiway","date":"05-11-2020, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:14:27-07:00","id":1387405,"title":"","content":"<b>Hank's Body Shop</b><ul><li>Auto mechanic garage, nestled inconspicuously between a thick copse of trees and several mostly abandoned buildings. If not for strategically placed signs and locals willing to give directions, you might not even be aware it's there. This is by design.</li> <li>The eponymous Hank performs regular auto repair and customization work, and does so quickly. He doesn't like &quot;normal&quot; clients hanging around.</li> <li>Primary business is with underworld types, as Hank specializes in adding hidden features to cars. Secret compartments, covert weapon holsters, and various &quot;Bond gadgets&quot; (machine guns in the headlights, oil slicks, etc).</li> <li>If it can be accomplished with mundane technology (or borderline technomancy), Hank can put it in a car and make it inconspicuous.</li> <li>Smugglers, drug dealers, and underground street racers are his primary clientele, and they pay top dollar.</li> <li>A hidden elevator on the garage floor can lower a vehicle to a secret basement level, where much of the heavy modification takes place.</li> <li>As insurance, Hank secretly maintains extensive records of his illicit work, in case he needs to bring everyone down with him. These records are booby trapped with incendiary devices, to burn the evidence and anyone who would try to steal it. (A nasty surprise to any incautious vampire burglar).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:22:19-07:00","id":1387567,"title":"","content":"something in each of my games is a small tavern, bar, some kind of establishment that is neutral ground ran by F***ing Tony, and don't you dare chance calling him Tony, regardless of how powerful you are, what your generation is, what powers you have, he will have you up against the wall by the neck slowly crushing your wind pipe making sure you get his warning on what his actual name is and only god could help you if you happen to be foolish enough to start a fight you and the one that picks up the fight may find yourselves in a whole world of hurt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:22:10-07:00","id":1388454,"title":"","content":"<b>Borderlands Cowboy Apparel</b><ul><li>Sells cowboy hats, cowboy boots, belts and belt buckles, jeans, rope, denim jackets, and various cowboy-themed knick-knacks.</li> <li>Old style country/western music playing over loud speaker.</li> <li>Afternoon hours, counter is manned by bored teenager, who barely feigns interest in &quot;cowboy stuff&quot;. Early and noon hours manned by septuagenarian gentleman with thick white mustache, a full ten gallon hat, an eyepatch, and nasty scars on his face and arms. If asked, says he got mauled by mountain lions while hunting.</li> <li>Hidden back room is the meeting place for a cell of the Tin Stars, a minor monster hunter organization operating in the American southwest. Founded in the 1800s by a group of sheriffs and deputies, the Tin Hats were always a small and deeply superstitious group, passing duties down through family lines. (They long ago learned to distrust anyone else; infiltrators and blood-addled spies burned them once too many times). The cell working out of this store has been less active for years now, but have ramped up activity now that a new generation is of age to start training.</li> <li>Lock-box in the back room contains a number of weapons - including revolvers loaded with silver bullets - and a number of spare tin star badges.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:19:04-07:00","id":1393464,"title":"","content":"<b>University Steam Tunnels</b><ul><li>Extensive network of utility tunnels and shafts beneath the local university campus.</li> <li>Connected to sewer system via poor municipal planning and weak concrete walls. An exposed pipe near the river provides relatively easy access from the surface.</li> <li>Most direct entrances sealed or locked by school administrators, after a student got lost in the tunnels and disappeared.</li> <li>Previously Nosferatu territory, the student in question was part of a LARPing group that used the tunnels in a game. Fell prey to a Nosferatu neonate (later executed). Resulting week-long search of the tunnels forced Nosferatu to abandon the steam tunnels and much of the surrounding sewer system. Lost student was never found.</li> <li>Decades later, gamers still make pilgrimage to the infamous steam tunnels, holding semi-annual LARPs, despite attempts by the school and police to stop it. Continued regular presence of individuals keep local Nosferatu wary of moving back in.</li> <li>A hidden cache of weapons, filing cabinets, and stashed bodies is said to exist, sealed, inside the steam tunnels. Nosferatu refuse to confirm or deny its existence.</li> <li>If the various entrances on campus weren't locked or sealed, the tunnels would make for a perfect means of getting around campus unseen.</li> <li>Sound of dripping, pumping water can be heard. Smells of mildew, rust, and rat droppings.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T22:20:54-07:00","id":1396614,"title":"","content":"<b>North Side Pet Supply</b><ul><li>Sells pet food, toys, accessories, etc. Many are clearance items bought on cheap from rotated out stock of chain stores. Anything not perishable will tend to be old.</li> <li>Small animals - hamsters, gerbils, small birds, occasionally kittens or puppies - for sale. Gets them from shady breeders, or whenever someone in the area posts having found a litter by happenstance. Borderline illegal, but the store keeps them healthy and fed enough. Store also sells mice, mostly as snake food (both live and frozen).</li> <li>Nestled between other businesses of greater note (basically next to whatever location the PCs may find themselves visiting). By default, neighbors are a law firm and a thrift store.</li> <li>During the day, counter maintained by a veterinary school drop-out, who had to leave school due to burnout. Is saving money to start classes again, works at the store because the owner is too desperate to keep an employee to refuse paying well. Wouldn't pass up a chance to make a quick buck, within most ethical constraints (they didn't get into veterinary work for the money).</li> <li>Owner is wanted for connection to a dog-fighting ring. Paranoid, in hiding under an assumed name. Is haunted by the memory of mutilated dogs (<i>as he should be</i>), has trouble sleeping.</li> <li>Store was broken into months ago, during the dead of night, multiple times in the span of a few weeks. Shelves of product disturbed, objects broken, several animals taken, with blood spilled on the scene.</li> <li>Unwilling to involve the cops (not that they'd help), owner has taken to maintaining vigil in the store during night hours. Had to hire an employee just to keep the store running. Sleeps fitfully in a hammock in the back room during the day. Carries a shotgun during night, kept in locker during day (combination lock).</li> <li>Sounds: Chirping birds, audible (but functional) AC, scurrying in metal cages, recorded lectures on a laptop, muffled snoring.</li> <li>Smells: Fur, feathers, bird seed, dog/cat food, animal feces, disinfectant.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T15:15:59-07:00","id":1415465,"title":"","content":"<b>Crowe Road Motel</b><ul><li>Situated within two hours drive from major city, in a small town with a few tourist attractions. Mostly a stop along the highway.</li> <li>Motel kept in reasonably good condition, for a motel. Preserves 70s era decor and wallpaper. Cheaper than the closest chain hotel.</li> <li>Owned by a set of ghouls in thrall to a Caitiff, who is also the regnant to the nearby diner. Caitiff has Obfuscate 3, and uses it to maintain a few faces, including a father and son pair (really just the same face kept aging to keep up with the times; will be replaced soon when the father &quot;retires to out of state&quot;).</li> <li>Caitiff the only permanent Kindred resident. Driven out of most cities, he settled here and took control of the motel. Keeps decor the same out of nostalgia.</li> <li>Motel acts as a common stop for Caitiff and Thin Bloods, as well as Gangrel or Ravnos willing to play nice and cause no trouble. Ask about the &quot;maximum shut-eye&quot; accommodations, to make the room more amenable to sensitive skin.</li> <li>Motel is an unofficial Elysium. Agents working for the nearby city's sheriff will hang around town, looking for known trouble-makers, or to warn Caitiff/Thin Bloods heading into the city to keep their visits brief. The motel owners have an understanding with these men. They let the Sheriff have a measure of influence here and contact them if Sabbat packs move through, in return they are left mostly alone and receive regular payment.</li> <li>A paranoid conspiracy theorist has been staying in one of the rooms for three weeks, afraid of some mysterious &quot;Them&quot; that's out to get him. If guns start going off, he's sure to crack and come out blasting himself.</li> <li>No black lights. Official motel policy.</li> <li>Smells of industrial cleaner and bacon, at all hours. Complimentary breakfast.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-25-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}